{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund skin removal surgery on the NHS following weight loss",
        "additional_details": "Excess skin after major weight loss can cause significant physical and psychological harm, including reduced mobility, skin problems, anxiety, low self-esteem and social isolation. Research shows body-contouring surgery can improve quality of life and wellbeing. Current NHS access is inconsistent and often depends on where a person lives. We believe recovery from obesity should include access to reconstructive surgery when excess skin causes significant harm.",
        "background": "Fund reconstructive skin removal surgery on the NHS for patients who have achieved substantial weight loss and are suffering significant physical or psychological harm because of excess skin.",
